  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1231 AM MST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nDry weather is forecast to prevail through the rest of the week. \nRidging will amplify over the Intermountain West, placing dry \nnorthwest flow over New Mexico. Temperatures will moderate somewhat \nthrough the week, rising a few degrees above normal by the end of \nthe week.\n\nModels are still split on the trajectory of a dry shortwave trough \nthat will dig into the desert southwest Thursday into Friday. Around \n60% of models show this Low moving into northern Mexico with no \nsensible impact to weather in New Mexico, although around 40% show \nthis weak trough traversing New Mexico and sending a weak Pacific \nfront across the region from northwest to southeast.\n\nThe polar jet stream if forecast to move further south over the \nweekend into the early part of the following week. While models are \nnot showing any significant storms, the pattern will become more \nconducive to wetter and cooler weather during the early part of \nDecember.",
